### Interview Tips

- Speak confidently and explain your thought process.
- Use **real project examples** wherever possible.
- If asked to compare tools (e.g., Playwright vs Selenium), focus on practical differences you've experienced.
- If you don't know an answer, say so honestly and explain how you would find or debug the solution.
- Keep your project explanation concise (2–3 minutes), then expand if the interviewer asks follow-up questions.

This job description aligns very closely with a **4+ years Playwright Automation Engineer** role, so expect most questions to revolve around **Playwright, JavaScript/TypeScript, API testing, framework design, Git, CI/CD, Agile, and your real project experience**.
